2.3 Testing and Verification
To verify the correctness of our function, we perform additional tests to check the stopping conditions.

The tests cover:

Maximum number of terms: the sequence should stop when it reaches the specified limit k.
Upper numerical threshold: the sequence should stop when a newly generated term exceeds the threshold i.
Termination at zero: the sequence should stop when it reaches zero.
These tests help ensure that the function follows the computational requirements of the project.

